        "text": "```python\ndef min_Swaps(str1, str2):\n    # If the strings are already the same, no swaps needed\n    if str1 == str2:\n        return 0\n    \n    # Count positions where the bits differ\n    diff_count = 0\n    for i in range(len(str1)):\n        if str1[i] != str2[i]:\n            diff_count += 1\n    \n    # For binary strings, if there are an even number of differences,\n    # we can fix them with diff_count // 2 swaps\n    # If odd, we need (diff_count + 1) // 2 swaps\n    # But actually, each swap can fix at most 2 differences\n    # So minimum swaps = diff_count // 2\n    # If diff_count is odd, we need one more swap to fix the last difference\n    # So total swaps = (diff_count + 1) // 2\n    \n    return (diff_count + 1) // 2\n```",
